ng."], ["Romex (NM cable)","Trade term \u2014 Romex (NM cable): Non-metallic sheathed cable for residential wiring."], ["EMT","Trade term \u2014 EMT: Electrical metallic tubing: thin-wall conduit bent with a bender."], ["Junction box","Trade term \u2014 Junction box: An enclosed box where wire splices are made; must stay accessible."], ["Wire gauge","Trade term \u2014 Wire gauge: AWG sizing: smaller numbers mean thicker wire and more current capacity."], ["Neutral wire","Trade term \u2014 Neutral wire: The current return path, normally white or gray."], ["Ground wire","Trade term \u2014 Ground wire: The safety path, bare or green, that trips breakers on faults."], ["Hot wire","Trade term \u2014 Hot wire: The energized conductor, usually black or red."], ["Three-way switch","Trade term \u2014 Three-way switch: Two switches controlling one light from different spots."], ["Load calculation","Trade term \u2014 Load calculation: Sizing service and circuits to the expected demand."], ["Knockout","Trade term \u2014 Knockout: The removable disc in boxes and panels for cable entry."], ["Fish tape","Trade term \u2014 Fish tape: The steel tape used to pull wire through conduit."], ["Megger","Trade term \u2014 Megger: An insulation resistance tester for finding damaged wire."], ["Torque spec","Trade term \u2014 Torque spec: The required tightness for lugs and terminals."], ["Lockout/tagout","Trade term \u2014 Lockout/tagout: The procedure locking energy sources off during work."]];
